minithor minikube delete — delete the minikube cluster

Usage: minithor [--profile <name>] minikube delete --confirm [--purge]

Options:
  --confirm        Required. Confirms you want to delete the cluster.
  --purge          Also remove ~/.minikube and ~/.kube, uninstall the minikube and
                   kubectl binaries, and prune unused container images (skipped while
                   other minikube profiles remain)
  -h, --help       Show this help message

Deletes only the selected profile's cluster, so other minikube clusters on this host are
left alone. This is irreversible.
EOF
}

usage_start() {
    cat <<EOF
minithor start — start a stopped minikube cluster

Usage: minithor start

Starts the selected profile's cluster with the driver it was created with,
corrects the kubeconfig API server address if needed, re-applies the node
proxy settings, kernel parameters, and registry host entry, and cleans up pods
