usage_deploy() {
    cat <<EOF
minithor deploy — deploy Thorium with the Thorium Helm charts

Usage: minithor [--namespace-prefix <prefix>] deploy [options]

Installs the infra-operators chart (once per cluster, skipping operators that already run)
and the thorium chart, waits for Thorium to be ready, installs thorctl, and imports the
default toolbox. Generated credentials are kept on redeploys, but no other option is: each
deploy renders the values from its own options alone (helm --reset-values), so repeat them
(--registry, --no-kibana, --values, ...) on every redeploy. A cluster runs one Thorium
deployment, so deploy refuses when one already exists under another namespace prefix.

Charts (default: ${CHART_REPO}/{thorium,infra-operators} at ${CHART_VERSION}):
  --chart <path|oci-ref>      The thorium chart: a local chart directory, a packaged
                              .tgz, or an oci:// reference
  --operators-chart <path|oci-ref>
                              The infra-operators chart (default: next to a local
                              --chart, or the matching oci:// reference)
  --chart-version <version>   Chart version for oci:// charts (default: ${CHART_VERSION})

Configuration:
  --user <name>               Admin username (default: the stored one on a redeploy, else
                              test)
  --password <pass>           Admin password (default: the stored one on a redeploy, else
                              INSECURE_DEV_PASSWORD)
  --rand-password             Let the chart generate the admin password on the first deploy;
                              a redeploy without --password keeps the stored one (see
                              'credentials'). Can't be combined with --password
  --version <tag>             Thorium image tag (default: the chart's appVersion)
  --registry                  Deploy a container registry at
                              docker-registry.<thorium namespace>.svc.cluster.local:${REGISTRY_PORT}
                              (the cluster must have been installed or last started
                              with the same --namespace-prefix so its runtime trusts it)
  --registry-user <name>      Enable registry basic auth for this user (implies
                              --registry; see 'credentials --all' for the password)
  --toolbox <path|url>        Toolbox to import (default: the toolbox on GitHub main);
                              fetched on this host
  --no-toolbox                Don't import a toolbox
  --banner <file>             Login banner text
  --docker-config <file>      .dockerconfigjson for pulling the Thorium image
  --bin <dir>                 Where to install thorctl (default: /usr/local/bin)
  --no-thorctl                Don't install thorctl
  --no-kibana                 Skip Kibana
  --proxy <url|none>          HTTP(S) proxy the scaler uses to reach registries such as ghcr.io
                              (default: the host's HTTPS_PROXY/HTTP_PROXY; none to leave it unset).
                              The scaler's no_proxy is only the cluster's own names and ranges:
                              localhost, 127.0.0.1, .svc, .svc.cluster.local, cluster.local,
                              control-plane.minikube.internal, the service and pod CIDRs, the
                              node subnet, and the in-cluster registry
  --no-proxy <list>           Extra comma-separated entries appended to the scaler's no_proxy
  --values <file>             Extra values file for the thorium chart (repeatable)
  --set <key.path=value>      Extra value for the thorium chart (repeatable), e.g.
                              operator.cluster.components.scaler=null to omit the scaler

Other:
  --skip-operators            Don't install or upgrade the infra-operators chart
  --timeout <seconds>         Timeout for each install and the readiness wait
                              (default: 1800)

Examples:
  minithor deploy
  minithor --namespace-prefix dev deploy --rand-password
  minithor deploy --chart ./thorium-1.8.1.tgz      # infra-operators-*.tgz alongside it
  minithor deploy --chart deploy/charts/thorium    # from a checkout
EOF
}

